# {{name}}

An Exeris frontend with no backend of its own. It runs the Exeris TypeScript generator,
`@exeris/codegen-ts`, on a backend's published contract artifact: the backend's `cap-manifest.json`
and the metadata of the entities it provides.

## Generate

Put the backend's contract artifact in `contracts/backend/`, or set the `path` of the `backend` peer
in `exeris-codegen.json` to where it is, then run:

```bash
npm install
npm run generate
```

The generator reads the contract artifacts `exeris-codegen.json` names, never a metadata directory
kept by hand. From peers alone it writes each peer's types, under `app/peers/<peer>/`, and no Angular
application. A backend writes `cap-manifest.json` only when it declares a `@CapabilityModule`, and
nothing resolves a contract artifact by its Maven coordinate yet.

